    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "End of terrace house with rear garden, a blank canvas brimming with potential, in superb location just a 10 minute stroll to Ballina Town Centre.\r\n\r\n63 Healy Terrace is an end-of-terrace property offering purchasers an exciting opportunity to create a home tailored entirely to their own tastes and requirements. \r\n\r\nWhile the property is in need of complete refurbishment, its excellent location, generous potential and enclosed rear garden make this an appealing prospect for owner-occupiers, renovators and investors alike.\r\n\r\nThe property would also likely qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant and the Repair and Leasing Scheme, potentially offering valuable financial assistance towards the cost of renovation.\r\n\r\nInternally, the property provides a blank canvas for transformation, allowing the successful purchaser to bring their own vision and style to this characterful home. \r\n\r\nTo the rear, the enclosed garden offers a private outdoor space, while the property also benefits from valuable rear access via a laneway, providing an additional entrance.\r\n\r\nBallina town centre is approximately a 10-minute walk away, placing an excellent range of local amenities within easy reach, including shops, schools, cafés, restaurants, pubs and sporting facilities. Ardnaree Sarsfields GAA Club is located to the rear of the property, while the town playground is also within approximately a 15-minute walk, making this a convenient setting for families and those looking to enjoy the amenities of the town on their doorstep.\r\n\r\nSituated at the mouth of the River Moy, Ballina is a vibrant town renowned for its rich history, culture and outstanding natural surroundings. The area offers an enviable selection of attractions and recreational amenities, including Belleek Woods, Ballina Golf Club and the world-famous River Moy, celebrated for its salmon fishing. The Ballina Arts Centre, Jackie Clarke Collection, Belleek Castle and the picturesque Quay Village further add to the town's appeal.\r\n\r\nFor those who enjoy coastal living and outdoor pursuits, the renowned seaside resort of Enniscrone is only a short drive away, offering approximately 5km of golden sandy beach, surfing and its famous seaweed baths. Killala and its scenic coastline are also within easy reach.\r\n\r\nCombining an excellent location with rear access, an enclosed garden and substantial scope for refurbishment, 63 Healy Terrace represents an exciting opportunity to create a home with long-term potential."
      },
